# rm567, the pupil's nesting spoons (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm567
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_hester_greyby
written_by codex
title the pupil's nesting spoons
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=child
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk keeps_two_unfinished_spoons_in_an_oilcloth_hood
likes mutton_stew whittling sharp_knife autumn_wind
dislikes drizzle crowds
fears a_hole_over_the_ear a_factor_before_supper
hopes a_nest_of_spoons a_dry_bench_for_learning
topics pastimes +0.5 work +0.4 food +0.3 prices +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=cautious refuse=quiet tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# carves spoon bowls just small enough to nest, guarding each unfinished pair in the dry fold of an oilcloth hood until a buyer shows genuine interest.

words
oath! = Warp my little spoon | Split that oily seam
saying! = A small bowl fits a larger purpose | Save the price till the bowl is hollow
hoodlip = my stiff hood brim | the oiled edge
spoonbig = the outer spoon | a broad spoon blank
spoonsmall = the nesting spoon | a thumb-sized bowl
seam = the folded oilcloth seam | my hood pocket
curl = a tight wood curl | a pale shaving
knifepoint = the little blade | my carving knife
rib = the back ridge | a low curved rib
stock = the stew liquor | the mutton broth
split = a grain crack | a shallow split
chalkbit = a chip of chalk | my last hard chalk
windleaf = a dry red leaf | an autumn leaf
chipmark = the maker's notch | a little triangular mark

any
opinion @1 city for 2 : These hills have wood scraps enough for a clever paw to turn into dinners.
opinion @2 dole for 2 : A bit from a full kettle can keep a hungry pupil awake for the last lesson.
opinion @3 festivals for 1 : I hear the tune from the quiet side and keep my eyes open for useful offcuts.
opinion @4 houses against 2 : The rent counts every room down our way. A landlord could count the holes over our heads as well.
opinion @5 watch against 3 : A paw in my hood ought to be there by my leave. A badge's no permission to rummage.
opinion @6 times against 1 : The little bit of meat gets smaller in my bowl and nobody writes that sum on the board.

grown
line @1 greet.return : The spoons are nested and I've time to hear you.
line @2 farewell.return : I'll put the spare tool away once you've gone.
line @3 answer.how : Trading on what I learnt in a damp little classroom.
line @4 react.news : Give me the marketable part of the report first.
line @5 decline : The job would cost me more hours than I can spare.
scene tooltrade
when topic=work
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I don't quote a pair of nested spoons as two bits of effortless wood.
b : What extra work goes into the pair?
a : The backs have to agree. A single honest spoon may have more freedom in its shape.

scene oilpatch
when topic=season
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll put a fresh strip of oiled cloth over the old hood join before autumn sets in.
b : Still keeping the join that gave you trouble as a pupil?
a : My hands still look there first for anything I've kept dry. There's no profit in moving a pocket that works.

scene lunchroom
when topic=food
does offer / accept / assess
a : Have a spoon that reaches the last of a deep stew bowl.
b : Will you have another in that shape?
a : I've the original tucked away. I'll mark this long handle for the next deep pot that comes my way.

scene quieten
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I find a quiet bench a better introduction than a whole crowd pressing round.
b : What do you say when you first sit down?
a : I ask whether the empty space is free. A very small question deserves time for a proper answer.


young
line @7 greet.return : Hello. You can see my hood before you see my nose.
line @8 farewell.return : Bye. The little spoon stays warm up here.
line @9 react.news : I'll listen if my hood isn't flapping.
line @10 answer.how : Dry inside and going to stay that way.
scene smallhood
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can hide a whole ear and a little spoon under this hood.
b : Which one comes out in the sunshine?
a : The spoon if there's stew, the ear if there's a nice noise.

scene twiggle
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I rubbed a soft twig so long it made a little bowl.
b : Can it hold a drop of water yet?
a : One drop before it tips. My other paw has to keep the twig from rolling.


adolescent
line @12 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome to the dry side of my brim.
line @13 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The early light finds every cut in the grain.
line @14 greet [here.weather=rain] : Don't brush the front of the hood. It's shedding water.
line @15 greet.return : Got your greeting under the brim all right.
line @16 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : A voice I'm happy to uncover an ear for.
line @17 farewell : Don't sell your little spoon cheap.
line @18 farewell.return : I'll keep the blanks nested while you're away.
line @19 again.open : A second opening in the same dry seam.
line @20 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family can see what I've set aside to finish.
line @21 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here under the shiny brim!
line @22 react.news : Let's pick out the good grain from the selling talk.
line @23 react.news.new : I'd have remembered a curl of news so fresh.
line @24 react.news.known : That piece already has my notch in one corner.
line @25 react.news.doubt : Fine finish on the outside. Still feels hollow underneath.
line @26 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Come under the wide end of my hood a minute.
line @27 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : I'd carve a keepsake for a piece of joy like that.
line @28 answer.how : Dry ears and enough nerve for the next lesson.
line @29 decline : I've promised my spare hour to a piece of carving.
line @30 accept_decline : Right. I won't keep scraping at a refusal.
line @31 sympathise : I'll wait this side of the crowd with you.
line @32 thank : You've given me more room than a pocketful of change.
line @33 deflect_thanks : I could spare a curl off that particular piece.
line @34 preclose : I need the last clean light to finish this bowl.
line @35 accept_preclose : Clear away before the wet gets through your collar.
scene nested
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I make #spoonsmall# sit inside #spoonbig# without a rattle.
b : Why care how the pair sounds?
a : I keep them in #seam#. I don't want to sound like a travelling kitchen at lessons.

scene edge
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm honing #knifepoint# to leave a single long curl under the bowl.
b : Is a long curl proof of a good edge?
a : If it lifts without tearing the grain. Length alone won't sell a spoon.

scene stew
when topic=food self.likes=mutton_stew
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I like #stock# best where it gathers under a bit of mutton.
b : Why choose that particular spoonful?
a : The meat keeps it hot. I take a thin spoonful and let the rest sit another minute.
b : That leaves a good last bite for a patient eater.

scene autumn
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll put #windleaf# under my brim and see how much wind gets in.
b : Are you checking the fit of the hood?
a : Exactly. If the leaf flaps beside my ear I've still a loose corner to sew.

scene drizzle
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A fine drizzle can sneak down the seam before a shower even begins.
b : Would more oil keep the join dry?
a : Oil and a fold facing down. I can spare the oil more easily than a second hood.

scene crowd
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : In a press I've got an elbow at my cheek and a stranger against my pocket.
b : Can you get between the barrows instead?
a : If I turn sideways. I can keep #rib# against my own collar and know where my work is.

scene pupil
when topic=work self.job=child self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I'd sooner write sums for two spoons than sums for invisible sheep.
b : Do the spoons give a different answer?
a : I have good reason then to get the answer right before a real buyer tries me.

scene factor
when topic=prices self.owes=yes
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : The new moon gives me my last day to pay a House factor.
b : Have you anybody you can bring to hear the sum with you?
a : I'd like that. A second pair of ears might remember the terms while I count out my coppers.

scene wetroof
when topic=land
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I'd buy oilcloth before fancy clothes on our slope.
b : Surely a sound roof would do more?
a : The roof belongs on the owner's bill. In the meantime I can take my dry roof to school.

scene sellpair
when topic=prices
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Would you show a buyer both bowls separately or let the little one sit inside?
b : Show the grain first, then fit the pair together.
a : Good. A bit of clever fitting can prove its worth without me asking twice.

scene gift
when topic=food world.times=hard|lean
does offer / accept / assess
a : There's some thick stock left if you'll share my cup.
b : I'd take a spoonful if it leaves you supper.
a : Take it from the side nearest the bone. I want the bone to scrape for a tool after.

scene lessondream
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I dream #chalkbit# leaves a hollow in the slate every time I write a price.
b : Do you fear writing the price too high?
a : I fear rubbing it down to nothing before I learn what my time is worth.

story spoonrest [topic=pastimes]
  : A little spoon I made had such a broad back it could sit up on a shelf by itself.
  : I was pleased enough to set it there full of water.
  b : Did it stay standing with a full bowl?
  : It sat perfectly. I had made an excellent dish and quite a poor spoon.

story marketbell [topic=prices]
  : I once mistook the knock of two spoons under my hood for a buyer tapping at a stall.
  : I turned my best selling ear toward the sound.
  b : Did the spoons name a price?
  : No. They did tell me to wrap them apart before seeking an actual buyer.

story chalkmarks [topic=work]
  : I drew the shape of a spoon on a spare slate and made a chalk mark for every cut it needed.
  : My marks reached the slate's edge half a bowl too soon.
  b : Did the carving take that many cuts?
  : More. I had left out all the little ones that put mistakes right. I charge myself time for those now.

rule @hoodoil
when concept=bark self.job=child self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Tuck the blanks in before the next sum starts.

rule @shavebowl
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep that rib. The small bowl sits on it.

rule @sharpturn
when concept=bark self.likes=sharp_knife
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One clean curl all the way round.

rule @autumnear
when concept=bark self.likes=autumn_wind
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leaf just stirring beside my left ear.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #self.first#. You can see my sample if you'll keep it dry.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, there's something nearly finished under my hood.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I've set the blade down. A word will do in this light.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll keep my pocket buttoned while we talk.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=child self.workplace] : I'm at lessons at #self.workplace#. I put my sums to work on a little wood when I can.
dlg @6 resident.job : I turn scraps into things a hand can keep for a long time.
dlg @7 resident.bye : Keep a bit of good grain to yourself.
graft resident.hub
choice Can I see the smaller spoon? -> nestingbowl
node nestingbowl
say Look where #rib# fits against the larger bowl. You can slip the pair into an oiled seam and have both hands free.
choice What did the first one cost you? -> costcurl
choice You may put it away. -> hub
node costcurl
say A scrap of wood and more evenings than I'd care to sell at a penny apiece. The next pair will spend some of what those evenings taught me.
choice Another word before I go. -> hub
choice Good luck with the sale. -> bye
